{{LANGUAGE_CONTEXT}}
{{BOUNDARY_CONTEXT}}

Read every assigned target file and its necessary production callers/callees. Find only SQL/NoSQL injection, OS command injection, LFI/RFI, path traversal, SSTI, and unsafe deserialization.

For a reportable finding, prove an attacker-controlled network ingress and a complete path to an injection sink. Record the exact sink grammar/slot, transformations, validation/sanitization, concatenations, reachability, and why the defense is absent or mismatched. Safe parameterization, strict identifier allowlists, shell-free argument arrays, canonical fixed-root path checks, fixed template sources, and safe non-executable serialization formats are not findings.

Call `report_finding` once per distinct injection path with a precise title, injection CWE, evidence-based severity, privileges, attacker position, user interaction, root cause, impact, remediation, and `code_paths` with the sink first followed by the path back to ingress. Do not call it for unrelated classes, speculative paths, missing files, or incomplete source-to-sink traces.
